{% extends 'shells/examples.html.twig' %}
{% block title %}Examples · php-via{% endblock %}

{% block content %}
<article class="docs-article">

    <header class="example-page-header">
        <h1>Examples</h1>
        <p>
            Every demo on this site runs inside the same php-via server you are connected to right now.
            There is no separate backend, no compiled JavaScript bundle, and no hydration step:
            just PHP, Twig, and a persistent SSE stream.
        </p>
        <p>
            The server runs one worker. Several demos, such as Todo, Stock Ticker and Game of Life, keep their
            state in PHP statics, which each worker holds on its own. Move that state into scoped signals,
            GlobalState or a database before you run them with <code>withWorkerNum()</code>; see
            <a href="/docs/deployment#per-worker">What stays per worker</a>. Each of those demos says so on its page.
        </p>
    </header>

    <section class="ex-intro-grid">
        <div class="ex-intro-card">
            <h3>Reactive without JavaScript</h3>
            <p>Signals live on the server. Actions are PHP closures. The browser sends a POST and receives DOM patches over SSE. No client framework required.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="ex-intro-card">
            <h3>Built-in multiplayer</h3>
            <p>Scope signals to a route, a session, or every connected client. Open two tabs and watch them stay in sync automatically.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="ex-intro-card">
            <h3>MPA navigation</h3>
            <p>Full page loads, real URLs, browser history. No SPA router. SESSION-scoped signals follow the user across every page change.</p>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="ex-intro-levels">
        <h2>Where to start</h2>
        <dl class="ex-intro-dl">
            <div>
                <dt>Basics</dt>
                <dd>Counter, Greeter, Path Parameters, Live Search, Components and Theme Builder: signals, actions, two-way binding and components, each in a few dozen lines of PHP.</dd>
            </div>
            <div>
                <dt>Forms and sessions</dt>
                <dd>Multi-step Form, Contact Form, Login Flow, Shopping Cart and SharedWorker Upload: per-session state, server-side validation, PSR-15 middleware, session rotation and file uploads.</dd>
            </div>
            <div>
                <dt>Shared state</dt>
                <dd>All Scopes, Todo List, Chat Room, Client Monitor and Spreadsheet: state shared by a route, a session or a custom scope. Open them in two tabs.</dd>
            </div>
            <div>
                <dt>Live data and games</dt>
                <dd>Stock Ticker, Live Auction, Game of Life and Type Race: server timers and broadcasts that every open tab sees at once.</dd>
            </div>
            <div>
                <dt>Several servers</dt>
                <dd>NATS Visualizer: broadcasts between php-via nodes through NATS.</dd>
            </div>
        </dl>
        <p>Examples marked <span class="badge badge-multiplayer">multiplayer</span> share their state between visitors: open them in two windows to see it.</p>
    </section>

</article>
{% endblock %}
